package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is a BYTE BUFFER (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5, §2.8): "A VALUE
// is anything a table field can hold ... `*bytes` ... (§2.5)". A buffer is a
// NODE, so the value is an ordinary pointer field of the generated entry and
// its storage is that field's own row, the eight-byte reference (§4.2). The
// handle is that SLOT. `*wstring` is refused under a map key by name and has no
// table here (§2.8, §11).

table Chunks
{
    blobs map[int32]*bytes // *bytes: an opaque buffer, under a signed key
    after int32
}
